WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.003
Simone Biles is back two years ago.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.604
The most decorated gymnast

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:05.305
of all time

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.573
stepped away from the sport

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.441
to see to her mental health needs.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.710
Maybe this video that much more welcome

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.078
seeing her back in action

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.547
practicing for this weekend's competition

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.382
near Chicago

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.984
her first since the 2021 Tokyo Olympics.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:19.753
And her last opportunity

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.087
to qualify for the U.S.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.589
Gymnastics Championship

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.557
Championships later this month.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:25.525
That's an important step

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.794
on the way to the 2024 Paris games.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.163
More now from CNN's Carolyn Marno.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.433
I guess I would describe myself

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.401
as confident

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:35.335
flying high

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:38.571
after five Olympic medals in 2016 in Rio

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.507
and an unprecedented ascension

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.042
to the top of the sport.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.144
I'm always in all when I watch her

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:46.046
sometimes I just think she's un human

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.048
just because she's just so amazing.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:48.915
Simone Biles

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.718
life took an unexpected detour that fall.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.720
USA Gymnastics was rocked

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.721
by revelations

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.157
of sexual abuse from longtime team

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.725
doctor Larry Nassar.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.793
Biles went public

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.995
with her own story in 2018

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.930
tweeting a statement which read in part

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.199
I know that this horrific experience

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.101
does not define me

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.270
at the 2021 Tokyo games.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.104
With the world

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:11.905
anticipating

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:14.140
another superhuman performance,

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.042
Biles showed her strength

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.644
outside of the competition

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.481
suffering from what she describes

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.515
as the twisties,

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.150
inexplicably losing her

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.852
bearings in the air.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.120
The girls tell me in training,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.388
my coaches saw me in training

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.490
like I physically couldn't do it safely,

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:31.324
and it's

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.726
because I was getting so lost in the air.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.562
The superstar gymnast withdrew

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:36.763
from five events

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.064
at the Tokyo games,

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:40.100
prioritizing her mental health

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.001
over her medal count

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.770
to bring the topic of mental health.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.404
I think

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.106
it should be talked about a lot more,

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.240
especially with athletes,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:47.907
because I know

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.209
some of us are going through

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:49.976
the same things

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:52.345
and we're always told to push through it.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.147
After returning home from Tokyo,

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.348
an emotional Biles

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.850
testified before the Senate

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.018
Judiciary Committee about the FBI's

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.687
handling of the sexual abuse

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.555
case against Nassar.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.991
To be clear, I blame Larry Nassar,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.726
and I also blame

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.431
an entire system

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:14.534
that enabled and perpetrated his abuse.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.670
Biles says she's been in therapy weekly

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.938
since stepping away.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.174
Now she's ready for a comeback.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:21.808
This weekend

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.709
marks her first

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:24.944
elite competition since 2021.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.180
She's aware of how influential

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.681
she continues to be

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.482
at the end of the day.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.583
We're not just entertainment.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.317
We're humans.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.085
And there are things

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.186
going on behind the scenes

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.487
that we're also trying to juggle

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.488
with as well.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.223
On top of sports

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.558
league gymnastics has helped

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.360
shape me and the people around by.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.362
I'm really excited about life

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.229
and what's to come

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.831
and how I've changed and evolved

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.332
as a person.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.434
Pamela I'm told that Biles is planning

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.068
on competing

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:49.969
in four events

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:50.970
in the Saturday's Core

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.905
Hydration Classic,

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.673
which has been sold out for weeks

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.041
ever since this news broke,

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:55.575
that she would be

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:56.876
coming back to the sport

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.411
and her return to elite

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.513
competition is also widely viewed

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.848
as the first step towards

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:02.582
a potential return

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.616
to the Olympic stage

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:04.784
that would be in Paris

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.452
in the summer of 2024.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.620
Pamela. Well, all right.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.821
Thanks so much.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.355
Joining us

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.323
now, sportscaster

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.125
and CNN contributor Bob Costas.

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.793
How exciting is this, Bob,

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.062
this return of Simone Biles?

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.664
And what will you be watching for

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:18.464
this weekend?

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:22.902
Well, it's very exciting.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.337
She's the best of all time

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.471
by acclamation.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.106
There's really no dispute.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.742
Some athletes establish their position.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:30.810
Historic Ali,

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.245
cumulatively,

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.880
even if she never competed

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.081
in another Olympics,

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.450
what she did in Rio in 2016

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.452
at the age of 19,

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.954
not just winning the events,

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.989
but executing maneuvers

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.391
that other gymnasts couldn't even try,

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.027
let alone do half as well.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.930
She was by acclimation the best ever.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.865
Now when we talk about the twisters,

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.068
as Carolyn mentioned,

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:55.702
there are a number

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.737
of overlapping aspects here.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.306
And that also connects to mental health.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.508
There's the abuse from Larry Nassar.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:03.610
There's all the pressure

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.246
put upon her as the face,

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.280
with all due respect

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.848
to Katie Ledecky and others

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:09.616
expected to be

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:12.318
the American face of the Tokyo Olympics

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.853
and those expectations.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:14.887
And then there's

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.723
the mind body disconnect

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.790
that may or may not

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.292
be affected by mental stress.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.060
But it stands to reason that it does,

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.128
at least to some extent,

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:23.529
that it played a role.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.765
And it's just too dangerous

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.533
when you have that disconnect.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.468
You could sustain

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.902
significant bodily injury.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:32.071
So all those things came into play

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.740
at once in Tokyo.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.142
Now, the best to ever do it is back.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.744
Assuming she can qualify

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:38.678
for the Olympic team

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.980
and there's something else here, Pamela.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.016
Nothing against Tokyo

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.517
as a site for an Olympics,

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.385
but we know

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:47.186
that it was in the midst of COVID

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:47.487
and there were

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.322
no spectators in the stands.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.424
That also applied in large part

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.358
to Beijing.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.093
But there were also misgivings

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.194
about the IOC

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.397
going back to Beijing for a second time.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.532
And all the human rights implications.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.667
So a lot of the joy

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.367
that surrounded

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.769
the Olympics wasn't there.

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:04.504
Now, this is a chance for the Olympics

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.005
to get its mojo back.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.041
Paris, what a wonderful setting

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.142
and an American audience.

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.710
I think we'll look forward to this

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.812
more than the last few Olympics.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.247
And among the reasons will be

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:15.181
that Simone Biles

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.717
is possibly back on that Olympic stage.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:18.351
Yes.

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:20.420
She creates so much of the anticipation.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.120
Right.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.522
And as we know, Bob,

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:23.790
since the Tokyo Olympics,

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.924
I mean, she's gotten married.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:27.126
She's building a life with her husband.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.027
What are the benefits

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.095
but also the challenges

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.230
for a dominant athlete like Simone Biles

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:33.032
taking that kind of break

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.067
from competition

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:36.903
Well, everyone's

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.339
individual circumstance is different.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.841
I think she needed that time away.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.409
It's pretty clear.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.911
I haven't been in touch with Simone

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:45.511
for a while.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.380
But I knew her pretty well

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.614
since I hosted the Olympics

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.450
in 2016 and kept track of her

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.584
leading up to that.

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:52.518
And subsequently,

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:53.920
we were at events together.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.155
She's a very bright young woman.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:59.459
It should be said that this is clearly

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:00.660
the last go around.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.397
27 is an advanced age for a modern

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.132
Olympic gymnast.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:07.233
Katie Ledecky,

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:07.900
the other most

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.335
famous American Olympian,

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.637
will be 27 next year as well.

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:13.306
But that's not such an advanced

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:14.707
age for a swimmer.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:17.944
So Simona was 19 when she did it in Rio.

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:20.446
She'll be 27 assuming she gets to Paris.

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.814
And we'll see what she's

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:22.849
capable of doing.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.684
But it's pretty clear

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:26.552
that she needed the time off

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.087
just to get herself together

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.355
in every respect.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:31.023
And then prime herself

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.992
for what may happen a year

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.193
from now in Paris.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:34.894
Yeah,

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:36.329
she just had so much courage

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:37.730
to be as open as she was

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.432
to take the time she needed. Right.

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.234
And she did receive backlash.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.068
Some backlash,

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:43.469
of course, for her decision in Tokyo.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.571
But she also received a lot of praise

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:46.739
for putting her safety

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:48.474
and her mental health first.

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:50.643
How impactful is her voice

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:52.345
among this generation

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:53.913
of athletes and beyond?

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.050
I think it is impactful, as is

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.951
Michael Phelps,

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.052
who's been very candid

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.788
about his own struggles

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:04.190
with depression or Kevin Love

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:07.059
in the NBA, or Naomi Osaka,

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.795
the tennis player.

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:11.197
There's less stigma attached to it.

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:13.099
There are still some people who react

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:15.234
with kind of an Old-School reaction, hey,

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:16.803
an athlete never quits.

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:18.271
Tough it out.

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:20.807
I think that there's an evolution now

00:07:20.807 --> 00:07:22.942
in our understanding and empathy

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:24.444
for these situations,

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:25.711
and it's moved forward

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:27.213
by those prominent athletes

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:28.314
who are willing to acknowledge

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:30.316
their own circumstances publicly.

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:31.317
Yeah, good for them.

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:33.352
Bob Costas, thank you. Great to see you.

